    <bpmn:process id="W_W1799" name="W1799. Vendor Co-Op Fund Reimbursement Claim &amp; Settlement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POP documentation submitted to vendor (W1798)
Frequency: ~50–100 claims/year
Volume: ~PHP 50–100M in annual co-op fund reimbursements
Owner: AP Manager
Participants: AP Manager, Marketing Team, Vendor
Source: workflow W1799 — Vendor Co-Op Fund Reimbursement Claim &amp; Settlement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1799_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1799_Lane1" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1799_Lane2" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1799_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1799_Start4" name="POP documentation submitted to vendor (W1798)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1799_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1799_Task5" name="Vendor reviews POP and approves/denies reimbursement: (a) typical review…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor reviews POP and approves/denies reimbursement: (a) typical review period: 30–60 days, (b) approval: vendor issues credit note or payment, (c) partial approval: vendor disputes portion of claim (documentation insufficient, expense not eligible, execution not per agreement), (d) denial: vendor rejects claim with reason
Responsible (R): Vendor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–60 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1799_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1799_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1799_Task6" name="AP Manager processes approved reimbursement: (a) credit note: applied to vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AP Manager processes approved reimbursement: (a) credit note: applied to vendor AP balance (reduces next payment to vendor), (b) cash payment: received in bank account; Treasury confirms and applies, (c) system records co-op fund income: debit cash/AP, credit co-op marketing income (contra-marketing expense)
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: Per settlement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1799_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1799_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1799_Task7" name="Dispute resolution: (a) if vendor partially denies: Marketing Team provides…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Dispute resolution: (a) if vendor partially denies: Marketing Team provides additional documentation or accepts denial, (b) if vendor fully denies: escalate to Category Manager for vendor relationship discussion, (c) unresolved disputes &gt; 90 days: written off; co-op fund income reduced accordingly
Responsible (R): AP Manager / Marketing Team
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1799_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1799_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1799_Task8" name="Quarterly: AP Manager reconciles co-op fund activity per vendor: (a) annual…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly: AP Manager reconciles co-op fund activity per vendor: (a) annual budget, (b) claimed amount, (c) approved and received, (d) pending, (e) denied, (f) remaining fund balance available
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1799_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1799_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1799_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1799_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1799_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-359 (ensure controlled execution — Co-Op Marketing &amp; Promotional Fund Management (PA-39.2).) | - operational: AP Manager review and approval gate; periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AP Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
