    <bpmn:process id="W_W1800" name="W1800. In-Store Vendor Display &amp; Endcap Program Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly/quarterly display rotation schedule
Frequency: Monthly display rotations
Volume: ~200 stores × ~10–15 paid display locations = 2,000–3,000 vendor-funded displays active at any time
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Managers, Store Managers, Vendors
Source: workflow W1800 — In-Store Vendor Display &amp; Endcap Program Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1800_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1800_Lane1" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1800_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1800_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1800_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1800_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1800_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1800_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1800_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1800_Start5" name="Monthly/quarterly display rotation schedule">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1800_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1800_Task6" name="VP Merchandising manages paid display program: (a) premium display locations…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Merchandising manages paid display program: (a) premium display locations identified per store: endcaps, feature tables, entrance displays, power aisle stacks, (b) pricing per display location per month (e.g., endcap: PHP 10–20K/month; entrance feature: PHP 30–50K/month), (c) vendors pay for premium placement via co-op fund, (d) display schedule rotated monthly or per promotional cycle
Responsible (R): Category Managers
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Monthly planning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1800_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1800_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1800_Task7" name="Store execution: (a) Store Manager receives display plan from merchandising…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store execution: (a) Store Manager receives display plan from merchandising, (b) sets up display per planogram and vendor-provided materials, (c) sends photo confirmation to Category Manager, (d) non-compliant stores flagged and corrected
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 days per rotation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1800_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1800_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1800_Task8" name="Performance tracking: Category Manager reviews display performance (sales lift…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Performance tracking: Category Manager reviews display performance (sales lift for displayed items vs. baseline); high-performing displays extended; underperforming displays rotated
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1800_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1800_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1800_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1800_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1800_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-359 (ensure controlled execution — Co-Op Marketing &amp; Promotional Fund Management (PA-39.2).) | - operational: VP Merchandising review and approval gate
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
