    <bpmn:process id="W_W1802" name="W1802. Co-Op Marketing ROI Analysis &amp; Vendor Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Post-campaign analysis; quarterly vendor business review
Frequency: Per campaign + quarterly aggregate
Volume: ~50–100 campaign analyses/year
Owner: FP&amp;A
Participants: FP&amp;A, CMO, Category Managers, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1802 — Co-Op Marketing ROI Analysis &amp; Vendor Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1802_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1802_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1802_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1802_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1802_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1802_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1802_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1802_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1802_Start4" name="Post-campaign analysis; quarterly vendor business review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1802_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1802_Task5" name="Per-campaign ROI analysis: (a) incremental sales during campaign period (vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Per-campaign ROI analysis: (a) incremental sales during campaign period (vs. baseline), (b) incremental gross margin (net of promotional markdown and BuildRight&#x27;s marketing spend), (c) vendor co-op funding received (or expected), (d) net cost to BuildRight = marketing spend − vendor funding, (e) ROI = incremental margin ÷ net cost, (f) campaign effectiveness metrics: reach, conversion rate, ATV lift
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A / Marketing Analytics
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 days/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1802_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1802_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1802_Task6" name="Quarterly aggregate: (a) total vendor co-op funding received vs. marketing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly aggregate: (a) total vendor co-op funding received vs. marketing spend, (b) co-op as % of total marketing budget, (c) ROI by vendor and by campaign type (catalog, digital, in-store display), (d) vendor ranking: highest co-op contributors and best ROI performers
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO / CMO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1802_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1802_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1802_Task7" name="Vendor business review: Category Managers present co-op marketing results to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor business review: Category Managers present co-op marketing results to key vendors: (a) campaign performance, (b) sales growth attributable to co-op activities, (c) proposal for next period co-op budget (increase for high-ROI activities), (d) strengthen vendor partnership based on mutual benefit
Responsible (R): Category Managers
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly per key vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1802_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1802_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1802_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1802_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1802_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-359 (ensure controlled execution — Co-Op Marketing &amp; Promotional Fund Management (PA-39.2).) | - operational: FP&amp;A review and approval gate
Owner: FP&amp;A</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
